<title>FRANCE: Cap Gemini to buy Portuguese software firm.</title>
<headline>Cap Gemini to buy Portuguese software firm.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cap Gemini, the French computer systems developer, said on Friday it planned to buy 50.6 percent of Portuguese software firm Geslogica in its first investment in Portugal.</p>
<p>Geslogica will remain 49.4-percent owned by Belgian group SAPEC and will be renamed Cap Gemini Portugal, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>It did not give a price for the acquisition.  </p>
<p>Le Figaro daily, anticipating the announcement earlier, said the Portuguese firm, created in 1992, had posted 1996 sales worth 50 million francs, up 50 percent in one year.</p>
</text>
